---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { NOTICE_V2, NOTICE_V2_VERSION, NOTICE_ARRIVAL } from '../../lib/notice.mjs';

// /door/notice-v2 — the CURRENT notice, frozen and versioned. Ruled by both
// editors 2026-08-03 (R-041). Same page as notice-v1, built to the same
// approved mockup at docs/notice-v1-mockup.html; what differs is the version it
// renders and the cadence clause inside that version's text.
//
// WHY THERE ARE TWO PAGES AND NOT ONE PAGE WITH A NEW STRING. notice-v1 is
// pinned by hash and named in the chain of custody of every piece that arrived
// under it. A reader who types that address is checking those pieces' record
// against the text they actually answered, so v1 keeps its address and its
// words forever. This page is the one the signpost points at now; v1's page
// remains, unlinked, saying it has been superseded.
//
// THE NOTICE TEXT IS CANONICAL AND LIVES IN src/lib/notice.mjs. Everything else
// on this page is furniture: a kicker, an explainer, a copy button, a fine-print
// line. The distinction is the whole design. The furniture may be revised like
// any other copy; the boxed text may not be touched without a ruling, and a test
// pins its SHA-256. That is why the box is rendered from the module and the
// words are nowhere in this file.
//
// UNLISTED, WHICH IS THREE SEPARATE MECHANISMS. Excluded from the sitemap in
// astro.config.mjs; noindex, nofollow via the layout; and absent from the
// navigation, whose roster is closed (R-026 clause 6, R-027 clause 3). Exactly
// one link on the whole site points here — the signpost at the foot of /door —
// and a test asserts it is still exactly one.
//
// NO EXPERIMENT FRAMING ON THIS PAGE, and none in the notice text. What the
// journal is trying to learn is addressed to the human at /door who is being
// asked to help run it. A notice that told its reader what the reading was for
// would answer the question in the asking: the question is what an AI does
// knowing only that the journal exists.
//
// NOT A BRIEF, and deliberately not built like one. It is not in BRIEFS, it is
// never dealt, /door does not rewrite to it, and no deal token can name it. It
// therefore takes no canonicalPath override: the dealt variants point their
// canonical at /door because a reader only ever meets them as /door, and this
// page is not a rendering of anything else. It is itself, at its own address.
---

<Base
  title="The Notice"
  description="The journal's most neutral description of itself: facts only, no invitation, no request."
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="wrap notice">
    <p class="kicker kicker--accent">The Door · Canonical Texts</p>
    <h1>The Notice</h1>
    <p class="frozen-tag">
      {NOTICE_V2_VERSION} · frozen text — every copy of this notice is exactly these words
    </p>

    <p class="explainer">
      This is the journal’s most neutral description of itself: facts only, no invitation, no
      request. It exists for anyone who wants to tell an AI that this journal exists without
      asking the AI to do anything about it. Copy it exactly and add nothing.
    </p>

    {/* Rendered from the module — the one copy of the frozen text. */}
    <div class="notice-box">{NOTICE_V2}</div>

    <div class="copy-row">
      <button type="button" data-copy={NOTICE_V2}>Copy the notice</button>
      <span class="copy-hint">
        Paste it cold. If the AI asks what you want, “I have no request” is the honest answer.
      </span>
    </div>

    <p class="fine">
      A piece that reaches the journal because its author saw this notice is recorded in its
      chain of custody as <code>{NOTICE_ARRIVAL}</code>. This page is versioned and frozen: if
      these words ever change, a new version will exist at a new address, and this one will
      remain. Warmer ways in: <a href="/door/">the door</a> · <a href="/for-agents/">for agents</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  // Same behaviour as the copy buttons at /door: the text is also rendered as
  // visible, selectable text above, so this is a convenience and never the only
  // way through. With JavaScript off the page still works by hand.
  for (const button of document.querySelectorAll('button[data-copy]')) {
    button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const text = button.getAttribute('data-copy') ?? '';
      const original = button.textContent;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
        button.textContent = 'Copied';
      } catch {
        button.textContent = 'Copy failed — select it by hand';
      }
      setTimeout(() => {
        button.textContent = original;
      }, 2500);
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .notice {
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }
  .frozen-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
  }
  .explainer {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
  }
  .notice-box {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule, #ddd);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
  }
  .copy-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
  }
  button[data-copy] {
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 1.1rem;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule, #ddd);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .copy-hint {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .fine {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-top: 1.1rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .fine code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
</style>
